Find the smallest integer \( n \) such that the expression \( 3n^2 + 8 \equiv 0 \pmod{7} \). The problem requires you to determine the smallest positive integer \( n \) that satisfies this congruence.  
(The smallest positive integer \( n \) should satisfy this congruence.)  
