Find the smallest positive integer \( n \) such that:
\[
\begin{cases}
7n \equiv 5 \pmod{23} \\
n \equiv 1 \pmod{3}
\end{cases}
\]

A rectangle \(R\) has an area of \(120\) square centimeters, and its length \(L\) and width \(W\) are positive integers. How many possible integer area equations involving \(x\) and \(y\) can be formed if each equation takes the form \((aL + bW)x - cy = 15\)? Find \(a + b + c\).
