Find all pairs of positive integers \((a, b)\) such that:
\[
\begin{cases}
|a - b| = n, & \text{where } n \text{ is a given positive integer} \\
a^2 + b^2 = m, & \text{where } m \text{ is a given positive integer}
\end{cases}
\]

For example, if \(n = 77\) and \(m = 3025\), what is the sum of all such pairs \((a, b)\)?

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 2 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{7} \\
x \equiv 4 \pmod{9}
\end{cases}
\]
